  "term": "Dalmane",
  "definition": "Dalmane is a brand name for flurazepam hydrochloride, a long-acting benzodiazepine that depresses central nervous system activity. It strengthens the inhibitory effects of GABA at GABA-A receptors, which reduces neuronal excitability and produces sedative and sleep-inducing effects.",
